' Lab 3 · Task 3 · Scenario 2 — Microsoft OAuth Session Creation
' and Author role elevation via the isAuthor flag on the User table.
' Unified human actor "User"; context role shown via note.
' External system "Microsoft OAuth" (lab2/adr/0005-oauth-for-authoring.md).

@startuml
title SchemaPostol - Scenario 2: Microsoft OAuth & Author Elevation (02-oauth)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

' ---------- Unified human actor + external system + DB entities ----------
actor "User" as HumanUser
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend" as BE
participant "Microsoft OAuth" as MS
database "User" as UserEntity
database "Session" as SessionEntity

note right of HumanUser
  Unified actor **User**.
  Context role: **Guest** starting the flow; after linking a
  licensed Minecraft account the user may be elevated to
  **Author** (`isAuthor` flag) or remains a **Registered User**.
end note

'
' ================= OAUTH SESSION CREATION =================
'
== Sign in with Microsoft ==

HumanUser -> FE : click "Sign in with Microsoft"
FE -> BE : GET /auth/oauth/microsoft (request authorize URL)
activate BE
BE -> BE : generate random state (CSRF protection)
BE --> FE : 200 OK {authorizeUrl, state}
deactivate BE

FE -> MS : redirect user to Microsoft authorization page
HumanUser -> MS : enter Microsoft credentials and consent
MS --> FE : redirect with temporary authorization code (+ state)
FE -> BE : POST /auth/oauth/microsoft/callback\n{code, state}
activate BE
alt state mismatch OR authorization code invalid
  BE --> FE : 401 Unauthorized {error: "OAuth authentication failed"}
else callback valid
  BE -> MS : exchange authorization code for token pair
  activate MS
  MS --> BE : {microsoftAccessToken, microsoftRefreshToken}
  deactivate MS
  BE -> MS : GET user profile (Bearer microsoftAccessToken)
  activate MS
  MS --> BE : Microsoft account data {nickname, email}
  deactivate MS

  ' ---- existence check + Author elevation via isAuthor ----
  BE -> UserEntity : findByEmail(email)
  activate UserEntity
  UserEntity --> BE : user {user_id, isAuthor} | null
  deactivate UserEntity
  alt user does not exist yet
    BE -> UserEntity : INSERT {user_id, nickname, email,\npassword_hash=null, isAuthor=true, created_at}
    activate UserEntity
    UserEntity --> BE : OK
    deactivate UserEntity
  else user exists and isAuthor = false
    BE -> UserEntity : UPDATE User SET isAuthor=true\nWHERE user_id = ...
    activate UserEntity
    UserEntity --> BE : OK
    deactivate UserEntity
  else user exists and isAuthor = true
    note right : already an Author - no change,\ncontinue the scenario
  end

  BE -> BE : generate refreshToken (7 days) +\naccessToken (15 min JWT)
  BE -> SessionEntity : createSession(user_id, hash(refreshToken),\nsession info: ip, user_agent)
  activate SessionEntity
  SessionEntity --> BE : session_id
  deactivate SessionEntity
  BE --> FE : 200 OK - accessToken (json) +\nrefreshToken (HttpOnly, Secure, Domain cookie)
end
deactivate BE
note over FE
  **Token storage:** JS keeps `accessToken` in memory; the
  browser automatically manages the `refreshToken` HttpOnly cookie.
end note
note over HumanUser
  **Author elevation (ADR-0005):** linking a licensed Microsoft/Mojang
  account flips `User.isAuthor` to true, promoting a Registered User to Author.
end note

@enduml